# 必考词 Unit20
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit20核心词汇

{{stall}}{{/stɔːl}}{{v./n. 停滞； stall；摊位}}{{The negotiations stalled over the issue of funding.}}
{{standard}}{{/ˈstændəd}}{{n./adj. 标准； standard；标准的}}{{The product meets international safety standards.}}
{{staple}}{{/ˈsteɪpl}}{{n./adj. 主要产品； staple；基本的}}{{Rice is a staple food in many Asian countries.}}
{{statistic}}{{/stəˈtɪstɪk}}{{n. 统计数据； statistic}}{{The statistics show a significant increase in sales.}}
{{status}}{{/ˈsteɪtəs}}{{n. 地位； status；状态}}{{The project's status is currently under review.}}
{{steady}}{{/ˈstedi}}{{adj./v. 稳定的； steady；使稳定}}{{The economy has shown steady growth.}}
{{stem}}{{/stem}}{{n./v. 茎； stem；阻止；源于}}{{Many problems stem from poor communication.}}
{{stereotype}}{{/ˈsteriətaɪp}}{{n./v. 刻板印象； stereotype；使固定}}{{We should challenge stereotypes about gender roles.}}
{{stern}}{{/stɜːn}}{{adj. 严厉的； stern；坚定的}}{{The teacher gave the students a stern warning.}}
{{stimulate}}{{/ˈstɪmjuleɪt}}{{v. 刺激； stimulate；激发}}{{The policy aims to stimulate economic growth.}}
{{stir}}{{/stɜːr}}{{v./n. 搅拌； stir；激起}}{{The controversy stirred up a heated debate.}}
{{straightforward}}{{/ˌstreɪtˈfɔːwəd}}{{adj. 直接的； straightforward；简单的}}{{The instructions are straightforward and easy to follow.}}
{{strain}}{{/streɪn}}{{n./v. 压力； strain；拉紧}}{{The workload is putting a strain on employees.}}
{{strategy}}{{/ˈstrætədʒi}}{{n. 策略； strategy；战略}}{{The company developed a new marketing strategy.}}
{{strengthen}}{{/ˈstreŋθn}}{{v. 加强； strengthen}}{{Exercise strengthens the muscles and bones.}}
{{stress}}{{/stres}}{{n./v. 压力； stress；强调}}{{She is under a lot of stress at work.}}
{{strict}}{{/strɪkt}}{{adj. 严格的； strict；严谨的}}{{The school has strict rules about uniforms.}}
{{stride}}{{/straɪd}}{{n./v. 大步； stride；进步}}{{The company has made great strides in technology.}}
{{strike}}{{/straɪk}}{{v./n. 罢工； strike；打击；袭击}}{{The workers went on strike for better pay.}}
{{string}}{{/strɪŋ}}{{n. 弦； string；一串}}{{There are several strings attached to the deal.}}
{{strip}}{{/strɪp}}{{v./n. 剥夺； strip；条；带}}{{The court stripped him of his rights.}}
{{strive}}{{/straɪv}}{{v. 努力； strive；奋斗}}{{We must strive for excellence in everything we do.}}
{{structure}}{{/ˈstrʌktʃər}}{{n./v. 结构； structure；组织}}{{The company restructured its management team.}}
{{submit}}{{/səbˈmɪt}}{{v. 提交； submit；服从}}{{Please submit your application by the deadline.}}
{{subordinate}}{{/səˈbɔːdɪnət}}{{adj./n. 下级的； subordinate；从属的}}{{The subordinate reported directly to the manager.}}
{{subsequent}}{{/ˈsʌbsɪkwənt}}{{adj. 随后的； subsequent}}{{In subsequent years, the company expanded rapidly.}}
{{substance}}{{/ˈsʌbstəns}}{{n. 物质； substance；实质}}{{The substance is harmful to the environment.}}
{{substantial}}{{/səbˈstænʃl}}{{adj. 大量的； substantial；实质的}}{{The company made a substantial investment in research.}}
{{substitute}}{{/ˈsʌbstɪtjuːt}}{{n./v. 替代品； substitute；代替}}{{You can substitute butter with olive oil.}}
{{subtle}}{{/ˈsʌtl}}{{adj. 微妙的； subtle； subtle}}{{There is a subtle difference between the two words.}}
{{succeed}}{{/səkˈsiːd}}{{v. 成功； succeed；继任}}{{She succeeded in getting the promotion.}}
{{sue}}{{/sjuː}}{{v. 起诉； sue}}{{The company was sued for discrimination.}}
{{sufficient}}{{/səˈfɪʃnt}}{{adj. 足够的； sufficient}}{{There is sufficient evidence to support the claim.}}
{{summit}}{{/ˈsʌmɪt}}{{n. 峰会； summit；顶点}}{{The leaders met at the G7 summit.}}
{{superficial}}{{/ˌsuːpəˈfɪʃl}}{{adj. 表面的； superficial；肤浅的}}{{His knowledge of the subject is superficial.}}
{{supplement}}{{/ˈsʌplɪment}}{{n./v. 补充； supplement；增刊}}{{She takes vitamin supplements every morning.}}
{{suppress}}{{/səˈpres}}{{v. 压制； suppress；抑制}}{{The government suppressed the protest.}}
{{surplus}}{{/ˈsɜːpləs}}{{n./adj. 剩余； surplus；过剩的}}{{The country has a trade surplus.}}
{{surrender}}{{/səˈrendər}}{{v./n. 投降； surrender；放弃}}{{The army surrendered after a long siege.}}
{{surveillance}}{{/sɜːˈveɪləns}}{{n. 监视； surveillance}}{{The area is under constant surveillance.}}
{{survey}}{{/ˈsɜːveɪ}}{{n./v. 调查； survey；测量}}{{The survey shows that most people support the policy.}}
{{survive}}{{/səˈvaɪv}}{{v. 幸存； survive；存活}}{{The company survived the economic downturn.}}
{{suspect}}{{/səˈspekt}}{{v./n. 怀疑； suspect；嫌疑犯}}{{Police suspect him of committing the crime.}}
{{suspend}}{{/səˈspend}}{{v. 暂停； suspend；悬挂}}{{The game was suspended due to rain.}}
{{sustain}}{{/səˈsteɪn}}{{v. 维持； sustain；遭受}}{{The company cannot sustain such high levels of debt.}}
{{symbol}}{{/ˈsɪmbl}}{{n. 象征； symbol；符号}}{{The dove is a symbol of peace.}}
{{sympathy}}{{/ˈsɪmpəθi}}{{n. 同情； sympathy；支持}}{{I have sympathy for people who have lost their jobs.}}
{{symptom}}{{/ˈsɪmptəm}}{{n. 症状； symptom；征兆}}{{Fever is a common symptom of the flu.}}
{{tackle}}{{/ˈtækl}}{{v./n. 处理； tackle；阻挡}}{{The government must tackle the issue of poverty.}}
{{target}}{{/ˈtɑːɡɪt}}{{n./v. 目标； target；针对}}{{The campaign targets young voters.}}
{{technique}}{{/tekˈniːk}}{{n. 技术； technique；方法}}{{She learned a new technique for painting.}}
{{temporary}}{{/ˈtemprəri}}{{adj. 临时的； temporary}}{{The arrangement is only temporary.}}
{{tendency}}{{/ˈtendənsi}}{{n. 趋势； tendency；倾向}}{{There is a tendency for prices to rise in winter.}}
{{tension}}{{/ˈtenʃn}}{{n. 紧张； tension；张力}}{{There is growing tension between the two countries.}}
{{terminal}}{{/ˈtɜːmɪnl}}{{adj./n. 晚期的； terminal；航站楼}}{{The patient was diagnosed with terminal cancer.}}
{{terminate}}{{/ˈtɜːmɪneɪt}}{{v. 终止； terminate}}{{The contract was terminated by mutual agreement.}}
{{territory}}{{/ˈterətɔːri}}{{n. 领土； territory；领域}}{{The country expanded its territory through conquest.}}
{{testify}}{{/ˈtestɪfaɪ}}{{v. 作证； testify；证明}}{{He was asked to testify in court.}}
{{theme}}{{/θiːm}}{{n. 主题； theme}}{{The theme of the conference is innovation.}}
{{theory}}{{/ˈθɪəri}}{{n. 理论； theory；学说}}{{The theory has been tested by many experiments.}}
{{therapy}}{{/ˈθerəpi}}{{n. 治疗； therapy；疗法}}{{She is receiving therapy for her condition.}}
{{thereby}}{{/ˌðeəˈbaɪ}}{{adv. 因此； thereby；从而}}{{He resigned, thereby avoiding further controversy.}}
{{thesis}}{{/ˈθiːsɪs}}{{n. 论文； thesis；论点}}{{She submitted her doctoral thesis last month.}}
{{thorough}}{{/ˈθʌrə}}{{adj. 彻底的； thorough；仔细的}}{{The police conducted a thorough investigation.}}
{{threat}}{{/θret}}{{n. 威胁； threat；恐吓}}{{Climate change poses a serious threat to the planet.}}
{{thrive}}{{/θraɪv}}{{v. 繁荣； thrive；茁壮成长}}{{The business has thrived in recent years.}}
{{tolerate}}{{/ˈtɒləreɪt}}{{v. 容忍； tolerate；忍受}}{{I won't tolerate any more delays.}}
{{torture}}{{/ˈtɔːtʃər}}{{n./v. 折磨； torture；酷刑}}{{The prisoners were subjected to torture.}}
{{tough}}{{/tʌf}}{{adj. 艰难的； tough；坚韧的}}{{It was a tough decision to make.}}
{{trace}}{{/treɪs}}{{v./n. 追溯； trace；痕迹}}{{The tradition can be traced back to the Middle Ages.}}
{{tradition}}{{/trəˈdɪʃn}}{{n. 传统； tradition}}{{The festival is a long-standing tradition.}}
{{tragic}}{{/ˈtrædʒɪk}}{{adj. 悲剧的； tragic}}{{The accident had tragic consequences.}}
{{trait}}{{/treɪt}}{{n. 特征； trait；特点}}{{Honesty is an admirable trait.}}
{{transaction}}{{/trænˈzækʃn}}{{n. 交易； transaction}}{{The transaction was completed successfully.}}
{{transform}}{{/trænsˈfɔːm}}{{v. 转变； transform；改造}}{{Technology has transformed the way we live.}}
{{transition}}{{/trænˈzɪʃn}}{{n./v. 过渡； transition；转变}}{{The transition to democracy was smooth.}}
{{transmit}}{{/trænzˈmɪt}}{{v. 传输； transmit；传播}}{{The disease can be transmitted through contact.}}
{{transparent}}{{/trænsˈpærənt}}{{adj. 透明的； transparent；坦率的}}{{The government should be more transparent about its policies.}}
{{transport}}{{/trænˈspɔːt}}{{v./n. 运输； transport；交通}}{{The goods were transported by rail.}}
{{trap}}{{/træp}}{{n./v. 陷阱； trap；困住}}{{The mouse was caught in a trap.}}
{{tremendous}}{{/trɪˈmendəs}}{{adj. 巨大的； tremendous；极好的}}{{The project requires a tremendous amount of effort.}}
{{trend}}{{/trend}}{{n. 趋势； trend；潮流}}{{There is a growing trend towards remote work.}}
{{trigger}}{{/ˈtrɪɡər}}{{v./n. 触发； trigger；扳机}}{{The event triggered a chain reaction.}}
{{triumph}}{{/ˈtraɪʌmf}}{{n./v. 胜利； triumph；成功}}{{The team's triumph was celebrated by fans worldwide.}}
{{trivial}}{{/ˈtrɪviəl}}{{adj. 琐碎的； trivial；不重要的}}{{Don't waste time on trivial matters.}}
{{tropical}}{{/ˈtrɒpɪkl}}{{adj. 热带的； tropical}}{{The island has a tropical climate.}}
{{tuition}}{{/tjuˈɪʃn}}{{n. 学费； tuition；教学}}{{University tuition fees have increased significantly.}}
{{turbulent}}{{/ˈtɜːbjələnt}}{{adj. 动荡的； turbulent；湍流的}}{{The country went through a turbulent period.}}
{{ultimate}}{{/ˈʌltɪmət}}{{adj. 最终的； ultimate；根本的}}{{The ultimate goal is to achieve world peace.}}
{{undergo}}{{/ˌʌndəˈɡəʊ}}{{v. 经历； undergo；接受}}{{The patient will undergo surgery tomorrow.}}
{{underlie}}{{/ˌʌndəˈlaɪ}}{{v. 构成…的基础； underlie}}{{Several factors underlie this decision.}}
{{undermine}}{{/ˌʌndəˈmaɪn}}{{v. 暗中破坏； undermine；削弱}}{{His actions undermined the team's confidence.}}
{{undertake}}{{/ˌʌndəˈteɪk}}{{v. 承担； undertake；从事}}{{She undertook the task with great enthusiasm.}}
{{unfold}}{{/ʌnˈfəʊld}}{{v. 展开； unfold；揭示}}{{The story unfolds over a period of twenty years.}}
{{uniform}}{{/ˈjuːnɪfɔːm}}{{n./adj. 制服； uniform；一致的}}{{The students must wear school uniforms.}}
{{unify}}{{/ˈjuːnɪfaɪ}}{{v. 统一； unify；使一致}}{{The leader sought to unify the divided nation.}}
{{unique}}{{/juˈniːk}}{{adj. 独特的； unique；唯一的}}{{Each person's fingerprint is unique.}}
{{universal}}{{/ˌjuːnɪˈvɜːsl}}{{adj. 普遍的； universal；全世界的}}{{Education is a universal right.}}
{{update}}{{/ʌpˈdeɪt}}{{v./n. 更新； update}}{{Please update your contact information.}}
{{upgrade}}{{/ʌpˈɡreɪd}}{{v./n. 升级； upgrade}}{{The company upgraded its computer systems.}}
{{uphold}}{{/ʌpˈhəʊld}}{{v. 支持； uphold；维护}}{{The court upheld the lower court's decision.}}
